  "output": "# Test Coverage Analysis — Canon (web)\n\n**Baseline: zero test coverage.** No `vitest`/`jest`, no `@testing-library/*`, no test script in `package.json`, no `*.test.ts(x)` files anywhere in the repo. Every gap below is therefore \"untested\" by definition — I've prioritized by risk (audit-trail integrity, money-shaped decisions like overrides/auto-apply, data corruption) rather than listing all ~150 functions.\n\n## 0. Infrastructure gap (blocks everything else)\n\nAdd Vitest (fast, native ESM/TS, works with React 19 + Next 16) + RTL for components. Server functions call `getDb()` directly with no repository seam, so DB-touching functions need either an integration DB or a `vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")`.\n\n```jsonc\n// package.json — add\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^3\", \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^4\",\n  \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16\", \"@testing-library/user-event\": \"^14\",\n  \"jsdom\": \"^25\"\n},\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest\", \"test:ui\": \"vitest --ui\" }\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: { environment: \"jsdom\", setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"] },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n## 1. Pure logic — highest value, zero excuse to skip\n\n### `lib/validate-value.ts` — `foldValue`, `checkObservedValue`\n\nThis is the guard against a human typing a hallucinated parent id into an override — the exact bug class the engine's `validate` node exists to prevent. It has zero coverage today.\n\n```ts\n// lib/validate-value.test.ts\nimport { describe, it, expect } from \"vitest\";\nimport { foldValue, checkObservedValue, observedValues } from \"@/lib/validate-value\";\n\ndescribe(\"foldValue\", () => {\n  it(\"folds case, whitespace and punctuation\", () => {\n    expect(foldValue(\"ACME-INC\")).toBe(foldValue(\"ACME INC\"));\n  });\n  it(\"strips a single legal suffix\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Acme Corp\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it(\"strips repeated suffixes (Pvt Ltd)\", () =>\n    expect(foldValue(\"Trellis Labs Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"trellis labs\"));\n  it(\"prefers the longest suffix match so 'pvt ltd' isn't left dangling 'pvt'\", () =>\n    expect(foldValue(\"Foo Pvt Ltd\")).toBe(\"foo\"));\n  it(\"keeps a value that IS entirely a suffix\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Ltd\")).toBe(\"ltd\"));\n  it(\"normalizes unicode (NFKD) before folding\", () => expect(foldValue(\"Ácme\")).toBe(\"acme\"));\n  it.todo(\"collapses internal punctuation to a single space, not none\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"checkObservedValue\", () => {\n  it(\"rejects an empty/whitespace-only candidate\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"  \", [\"ACC-1\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"rejects when neither side holds a value\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-1\", []).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it(\"accepts an exact match\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"ACC-1\", [\"ACC-1\", \"ACC-2\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"ACC-1\" });\n  });\n  it(\"accepts a legal normalization and returns the OBSERVED form, not the typed one\", () => {\n    const r = checkObservedValue(\"acme inc\", [\"Acme Corp\"]);\n    expect(r).toEqual({ ok: true, matches: \"Acme Corp\" });\n  });\n  it(\"rejects an invented value that folds to nothing observed\", () => {\n    expect(checkObservedValue(\"ACC-9999\", [\"ACC-1\", \"ACC-2\"]).ok).toBe(false);\n  });\n  it.todo(\"ignores blank entries within `observed` when reporting the reason list\");\n});\n\ndescribe(\"observedValues\", () => {\n  it(\"flattens both sides and drops blanks\", () => {\n    expect(observedValues({ a: { values: [\"x\", \"\"] }, b: { values: [] } })).toEqual([\"x\"]);\n  });\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/diff-chars.ts` — `diffSegments`\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"diffSegments\", () => {\n  it(\"puts everything in