tatus has two underscores\");\n});\n```\n\n### `lib/uuid.ts`, `lib/cn.ts`, `lib/reviewer-label.ts` — trivial but zero coverage\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"isUuid\", () => {\n  it.each([\"not-a-uuid\", \"banana\", \"\", \"  \"])(\"rejects %s\", (v) => expect(isUuid(v)).toBe(false));\n  it(\"accepts a v4 uuid, case-insensitively\", () => expect(isUuid(\"A41FBB00-0000-4000-8000-000000000000\")).toBe(true));\n});\ndescribe(\"reviewerLabel\", () => {\n  it(\"prefers username over email\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"falls back to email when no username\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"falls back to the stable id when user is null\", () => expect(reviewerLabel(null, \"user_1\")).toBe(\"user_1\"));\n});\n```\n\n### `types/rules.ts` — `orderRulesByEvaluation`, `ruleSpecificity`\n\nDrives what the policy editor shows as \"the order that will actually run\" — a wrong ordering here silently misleads an operator authoring survivorship policy.\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"orderRulesByEvaluation\", () => {\n  it(\"orders exact-field+exact-entity above either wildcard\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"keeps author order for ties (stable sort)\", () => { /* two rules with identical specificity */ });\n  it(\"places the fully-wildcard fallback rule last\", () => { /* ... */ });\n});\n```\n\n### `types/run.ts` — `failedStage`, `isStatKnown`, `runStageIndex`\n\n```ts\ndescribe(\"failedStage\", () => {\n  it(\"reads stage= off the error string, case-insensitively\", () => { /* ... */ });\n  it(\"maps 'dispatch' to the 'queued' stage\", () => { /* the EngineDispatch failure path */ });\n  it(\"returns null when the error has no stage= token\", () => expect(failedStage(\"boom\")).toBeNull());\n  it(\"returns null when error is null\", () => expect(failedStage(null)).toBeNull());\n  it.todo(\"returns null for a verb not present in byVerb, rather than throwing\");\n});\ndescribe(\"isStatKnown\", () => {\n  it(\"treats a failed run as having every stat knowable\", () => { /* status: 'failed' */ });\n  it