        "content": "\nAdd Vitest (fast, native ESM/TS, works with React 19 + Next 16) + RTL for components. Server functions call `getDb()` directly with no repository seam, so DB-touching functions need either an integration DB or a `vi.mock(\"@/lib/db\")`.\n\n```jsonc\n// package.json — add\n\"devDependencies\": {\n  \"vitest\": \"^3\", \"@vitejs/plugin-react\": \"^4\",\n  \"@testing-library/react\": \"^16\", \"@testing-library/user-event\": \"^14\",\n  \"jsdom\": \"^25\"\n},\n\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"vitest\", \"test:ui\": \"vitest --ui\" }\n```\n\n```ts\n// vitest.config.ts\nimport { defineConfig } from \"vitest/config\";\nimport react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\";\nimport path from \"path\";\n\nexport default defineConfig({\n  plugins: [react()],\n  test: { environment: \"jsdom\", setupFiles: [\"./vitest.setup.ts\"] },\n  resolve: { alias: { \"@\": path.resolve(__dirname, \".\") } },\n});\n```\n\n---\n\n",
