        "content": "\n| Scenario | Where | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Engine rejects run dispatch after row insert | `POST /api/runs` | Untested — the one case the code goes out of its way to handle correctly (wireframe 1h) |\n| Engine returns 200 with wrong shape (contract break) | `engine.ts` | Untested |\n| `fetch` throws (offline) from the browser | `lib/api-client.ts` | Untested |\n| Non-JSON error body from a route handler | `lib/api-client.ts` | Untested |\n| Two concurrent `createRulesetVersion` calls | `rulesets.ts` | Untested (advisory lock has no test) |\n| Override value that's neither observed nor a legal fold | `validate-value.ts` + route | Untested |\n| Approving a conflict with no proposed value | `conflicts.ts::recordReview` | Untested |\n| Malformed JSON body to any POST/PATCH | `respond.ts::parseJson` | Untested |\n| `runId`/`conflictId` that's syntactically not a UUID | multiple routes | Untested (the whole point of `isUuid` pre-checks) |\n\n---\n\n",
        "level": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "6. Integration test gaps (no unit test can cover these)",
        "content": "1. **End-to-end review flow**: create source → create ruleset → start run → poll status to `complete` → approve/reject/override conflicts → export → verify the exported hierarchy/decisions match what was actually decided. Nothing exercises this path today.\n2. **Audit trail completeness**: no test asserts that a full session of N reviews produces exactly N `human_*` audit rows with correct `previousStatus` chaining — the append-only guarantee is a written comment, not a tested invariant.\n3. **Engine contract drift**: `engineStartRunResponseSchema` / `engineRunStatusSchema` are validated at runtime but never tested against a realistic engine fixture — a schema/engine mismatch is currently only caught in production.\n4. **Auth boundary**: `proxy.ts` protects every route except `/`, `/sign-in`, `/sign-up`; there's no test (e.g. Playwright) proving an unauthenticated request to `/api/runs` is actually rejected, or that a static asset isn't accidentally gated.\n5. **Cross-layer reproducibility**: `lib/validate-value.ts`'s comment explicitly says it \"mirrors `engine/agent/graph.py::validate`\" and must stay in lockstep — there is no test (even a golden-fixture test) that would catch the two implementations drifting apart.\n\n---\n\n**Suggested order of attack**: (1) wire up Vitest, (2) `lib/validate-value.ts` + `lib/server/conflicts.ts::recordReview` since they gate what enters the permanent audit trail, (3) route-handler validation tests (cheap, high bug-catch rate), (4) the `use-review`/`ConflictQueue` keyboard layer since it's the primary reviewer workflow, (5) integration/concurrency tests last.",
        "level": 2
      }
    ],
